{
  "id": "m2l2",
  "title": {
    "es": "El bucle while",
    "en": "The while loop"
  },
  "theory": {
    "es": [
      {
        "type": "heading",
        "value": "Repetir mientras se cumpla algo"
      },
      {
        "type": "text",
        "value": "El bucle `while` repite un bloque **mientras** su condición sea verdadera. Antes de cada vuelta comprueba la condición; cuando deja de cumplirse, sale."
      },
      {
        "type": "code",
        "value": [
          "i = 1",
          "while i <= 3:",
          "    print(i)",
          "    i = i + 1"
        ]
      },
      {
        "type": "output",
        "value": [
          "1",
          "2",
          "3"
        ]
      },
      {
        "type": "note",
        "value": "Si la condición nunca se vuelve falsa, tienes un **bucle infinito**. Asegúrate de que algo cambie dentro del bucle (aquí, `i` aumenta) para que termine."
      },
      {
        "type": "heading",
        "value": "Acumuladores"
      },
      {
        "type": "text",
        "value": "Un patrón muy común es acumular un resultado en una variable que actualizas en cada vuelta."
      },
      {
        "type": "code",
        "value": [
          "total = 0",
          "n = 1",
          "while n <= 5:",
          "    total = total + n",
          "    n = n + 1",
          "print(total)"
        ]
      },
      {
        "type": "output",
        "value": [
          "15"
        ]
      },
      {
        "type": "heading",
        "value": "break y continue"
      },
      {
        "type": "text",
        "value": "`break` sale del bucle inmediatamente. `continue` salta el resto de la vuelta actual y pasa a la siguiente."
      },
      {
        "type": "code",
        "value": [
          "n = 0",
          "while True:",
          "    n = n + 1",
          "    if n == 3:",
          "        continue",
          "    if n > 5:",
          "        break",
          "    print(n)"
        ]
      },
      {
        "type": "output",
        "value": [
          "1",
          "2",
          "4",
          "5"
        ]
      },
      {
        "type": "text",
        "value": "`while True:` con un `break` dentro es una forma habitual de repetir hasta que ocurra una condición de salida."
      }
    ],
    "en": [
      {
        "type": "heading",
        "value": "Repeat while something holds"
      },
      {
        "type": "text",
        "value": "The `while` loop repeats a block **as long as** its condition is true. Before each pass it checks the condition; when it no longer holds, it exits."
      },
      {
        "type": "code",
        "value": [
          "i = 1",
          "while i <= 3:",
          "    print(i)",
          "    i = i + 1"
        ]
      },
      {
        "type": "output",
        "value": [
          "1",
          "2",
          "3"
        ]
      },
      {
        "type": "note",
        "value": "If the condition never becomes false, you have an **infinite loop**. Make sure something changes inside the loop (here, `i` increases) so it ends."
      },
      {
        "type": "heading",
        "value": "Accumulators"
      },
      {
        "type": "text",
        "value": "A very common pattern is to accumulate a result in a variable you update each pass."
      },
      {
        "type": "code",
        "value": [
          "total = 0",
          "n = 1",
          "while n <= 5:",
          "    total = total + n",
          "    n = n + 1",
          "print(total)"
        ]
      },
      {
        "type": "output",
        "value": [
          "15"
        ]
      },
      {
        "type": "heading",
        "value": "break and continue"
      },
      {
        "type": "text",
        "value": "`break` exits the loop immediately. `continue` skips the rest of the current pass and moves to the next."
      },
      {
        "type": "code",
        "value": [
          "n = 0",
          "while True:",
          "    n = n + 1",
          "    if n == 3:",
          "        continue",
          "    if n > 5:",
          "        break",
          "    print(n)"
        ]
      },
      {
        "type": "output",
        "value": [
          "1",
          "2",
          "4",
          "5"
        ]
      },
      {
        "type": "text",
        "value": "`while True:` with a `break` inside is a common way to repeat until an exit condition occurs."
      }
    ]
  },
  "exercises": [
    {
      "id": "m2l2e1",
      "prompt": {
        "es": "Define `suma_hasta(n)` que devuelva la suma `1 + 2 + ... + n` usando un bucle `while`. Si `n` es 0 o negativo, devuelve 0.",
        "en": "Define `suma_hasta(n)` returning the sum `1 + 2 + ... + n` using a `while` loop. If `n` is 0 or negative, return 0."
      },
      "starter_code": [
        "def suma_hasta(n):",
        "    total = 0",
        "    # completa el bucle while",
        "    return total"
      ],
      "solution": [
        "def suma_hasta(n):",
        "    total = 0",
        "    i = 1",
        "    while i <= n:",
        "        total = total + i",
        "        i = i + 1",
        "    return total"
      ],
      "hints": {
        "es": [
          "Usa un acumulador 'total' y una variable 'i' que avance.",
          "El bucle corre mientras i <= n."
        ],
        "en": [
          "Use an accumulator 'total' and a counter 'i'.",
          "The loop runs while i <= n."
        ]
      },
      "tests": [
        {
          "type": "function",
          "name": "suma_hasta",
          "function": "suma_hasta",
          "cases": [
            {
              "args": [
                5
              ],
              "expected": 15
            },
            {
              "args": [
                1
              ],
              "expected": 1
            },
            {
              "args": [
                0
              ],
              "expected": 0
            },
            {
              "args": [
                100
              ],
              "expected": 5050
            }
          ]
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "m2l2e2",
      "prompt": {
        "es": "Define `cuenta_atras(n)` que devuelva una **lista** con los números desde `n` hasta `1` en orden descendente. Ejemplo: `cuenta_atras(3)` -> `[3, 2, 1]`.",
        "en": "Define `cuenta_atras(n)` returning a **list** with the numbers from `n` down to `1` in descending order. Example: `cuenta_atras(3)` -> `[3, 2, 1]`."
      },
      "starter_code": [
        "def cuenta_atras(n):",
        "    resultado = []",
        "    # usa un while",
        "    return resultado"
      ],
      "solution": [
        "def cuenta_atras(n):",
        "    resultado = []",
        "    while n >= 1:",
        "        resultado.append(n)",
        "        n = n - 1",
        "    return resultado"
      ],
      "hints": {
        "es": [
          "Empieza con una lista vacía y usa .append(n).",
          "Decrementa n en cada vuelta: n = n - 1."
        ],
        "en": [
          "Start with an empty list and use .append(n).",
          "Decrease n each pass: n = n - 1."
        ]
      },
      "tests": [
        {
          "type": "function",
          "name": "cuenta_atras",
          "function": "cuenta_atras",
          "cases": [
            {
              "args": [
                3
              ],
              "expected": [
                3,
                2,
                1
              ]
            },
            {
              "args": [
                1
              ],
              "expected": [
                1
              ]
            },
            {
              "args": [
                0
              ],
              "expected": []
            }
          ]
        }
      ]
    }
  ]
}